t uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Functions public  function get_accumulation_mode (hconfig, rc) result(accumulation_mode) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ESMF_HConfig ), intent(in) :: hconfig integer, intent(out), optional :: rc Return Value character(len=:), allocatable public  function detect_geom (bundle, collection_name, rc) result(geom) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(ESMF_FieldBundle), intent(inout) :: bundle character(len=*), intent(in) :: collection_name integer, intent(out), optional :: rc Return Value type( ESMF_Geom ) public  function make_geom (hconfig, rc) result(geom) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ESMF_HConfig ), intent(inout) :: hconfig integer, intent(out), optional :: rc Return Value type( ESMF_Geom ) public  function append_to_time_vec (time_vec, time, rc) result(new_time_vec) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ESMF_Time ), intent(in) :: time_vec (:) type( ESMF_Time ), intent(in) :: time integer, intent(out), optional :: rc Return Value type( ESMF_Time ), allocatable, (:) public  function compute_file_timestamp (accumulation_mode, current_time, timestep, rc) result(file_timestamp) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: accumulation_mode type( ESMF_Time ), intent(in) :: current_time type( ESMF_TimeInterval ), intent(in) :: timestep integer, intent(out), optional :: rc Return Value type( ESMF_Time ) public  function set_start_stop_time (clock, hconfig, rc) result(start_stop_time) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ESMF_Clock ), intent(inout) :: clock type( ESMF_HConfig ), intent(in) :: hconfig integer, intent(out), optional :: rc Return Value type( ESMF_Time ), (2) public  function get_frequency (hconfig, rc) result(frequency) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ESMF_HConfig ), intent(in) :: hconfig integer, intent(out), optional :: rc Return Value type( ESMF_TimeInterval ) public  function create_output_bundle (hconfig, import_state, rc) result(bundle) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ESMF_HConfig ), intent(in) :: hconfig type( ESMF_State ), intent(in) :: import_state integer, intent(out), optional :: rc Return Value type(ESMF_FieldBundle) public  function get_expression_variables (expression, rc) result(variables) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name character(len=*), intent(in) :: expression integer, intent(out), optional :: rc Return Value type(StringVector) Subroutines public  subroutine get_real_time_vector (initial_time, esmf_time_vector, real_time_vector, rc) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ESMF_Time ), intent(in) :: initial_time type( ESMF_Time ), intent(in) :: esmf_time_vector (:) real, intent(out), allocatable :: real_time_vector (:) integer, intent(out), optional :: rc public  subroutine register_imports (gridcomp, hconfig, rc) Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ESMF_GridComp ), intent(inout) :: gridcomp type( ESMF_HConfig ), intent(in) :: hconfig integer, intent(out), optional :: rc","tags":"","url":"module/mapl_historycollectiongridcomp_private_mod.html"},{"title":"mapl_ArrayReductions_mod – MAPL","text":"MODULE: mapl_ArrayReductions Author: GMAO SI-Team mapl_ArrayReductions — Parallel collective reductions over arrays This module provides MPI-based global reduction operations over Fortran\n arrays: MaxMin : global parallel max and min of an array AreaMean : global parallel area-weighted mean of a 2-D array Previously these lived in the single-entity modules MaxMin and AreaMean (in utils/arrays/ ). They were consolidated here because\n both are MPI-dependent parallel reductions and belong in MAPL.mp_utils ,\n and because single-public-symbol modules create naming conflicts under\n Intel Fortran’s case-insensitive module namespace rules (#4944).\n The macros here are intended to simplify the process of\n accessing the per-gc private state via ESMF. Simple exception handling macros for MAPL. Short hand for declaring key variables Automatic exception hanler Try & catch exception functionality; the rc macro is similar\n to the RC=STATUS); _VERIFY(STATUS macro above but it does not invole the _VERIFY(STATUS)\n macro. Instead, it jumps out of the TRY block. Raising exceptions Pre-defined MAPL error codes The MAPL_ErrLog must be defined after MAPL_Exceptions The error logging may eventually evolve into a module based\n on the ESMF logger.  For now these macros provide simple\n traceback capability.\n new\n New\n Assumes status is passed back in dummy called “rc”\n Assumes “/home/runner/work/MAPL/MAPL/include/MAPL_ErrLog.h” and 130 are appropriate\n Old\n The error logging may eventually evolve into a module based\n on the ESMF logger.  For now these macros provide simple\n traceback capability.\n new\n New\n Assumes status is passed back in dummy called “rc”\n Assumes “/home/runner/work/MAPL/MAPL/include/MAPL_ErrLog.h” and 130 are appropriate\n Old\n The following macro causes a variable to appear to be “used”\n according to the compiler.  This is a kludge to avoid excessive\n warnings.  In most cases, a better fix would be to modify the the\n procedure interface, but it is impractical in the short term. Note that the conditional is never satisfied and a reasonable\n compiler will optimize the line away.  (Hopefully without\n reintroducing the warning!) Compute the global parallel max and min of a Fortran array.\n Returns a 2-element array [max, min]. Uses mapl_ErrorHandling_mod iso_fortran_env MAPL_Constants mpi module~~mapl_arrayreductions_mod~~UsesGraph module~mapl_arrayreductions_mod mapl_ArrayReductions_mod iso_fortran_env iso_fortran_env module~mapl_arrayreductions_mod->iso_fortran_env module~mapl_constants MAPL_Constants module~mapl_arrayreductions_mod->module~mapl_constants module~mapl_errorhandling_mod mapl_ErrorHandling_mod module~mapl_arrayreductions_mod->module~mapl_errorhandling_mod mpi mpi module~mapl_arrayreductions_mod->mpi module~mapl_earthatmosphericconstants_mod mapl_EarthAtmosphericConstants_mod module~mapl_constants->module~mapl_earthatmosphericconstants_mod module~mapl_earthconstants_mod mapl_EarthConstants_mod module~mapl_constants->module~mapl_earthconstants_mod module~mapl_internalconstants_mod mapl_InternalConstants_mod module~mapl_constants->module~mapl_internalconstants_mod module~mapl_mathconstants_mod mapl_MathConstants_mod module~mapl_constants->module~mapl_mathconstants_mod module~mapl_physicalconstants_mod mapl_PhysicalConstants_mod module~mapl_constants->module~mapl_physicalconstants_mod module~mapl_throw_mod mapl_Throw_mod module~mapl_errorhandling_mod->module~mapl_throw_mod module~mapl_earthatmosphericconstants_mod->module~mapl_physicalconstants_mod module~mapl_earthconstants_mod->iso_fortran_env module~mapl_earthconstants_mod->module~mapl_mathconstants_mod module~mapl_internalconstants_mod->iso_fortran_env module~mapl_mathconstants_mod->iso_fortran_env Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~mapl_arrayreductions_mod~~UsedByGraph module~mapl_arrayreductions_mod mapl_ArrayReductions_mod module~mapl_mp_utils_api mapl_mp_utils_api module~mapl_mp_utils_api->module~mapl_arrayreductions_mod module~mapl_simplebundlemod_impl_mod mapl_SimpleBundleMod_impl_mod module~mapl_simplebundlemod_impl_mod->module~mapl_arrayreductions_mod module~mapl MAPL module~mapl->module~mapl_mp_utils_api module~mapl_base_api mapl_base_api module~mapl_