ource, destination) Type-Bound Procedures procedure, public :: activate procedure, public :: connect procedure, public :: connect_export_to_export procedure, public :: get_destination procedure, public :: get_source","tags":"","url":"module/mapl_reexportconnection_mod.html"},{"title":"mapl_SimpleBundleMod_impl_mod – MAPL","text":"MODULE: MAPL_SimpleBundleMod Author: GMAO SI-Team The module MAPL_SimpleBundleMod implements a wrapper class around the\n ESMF_FieldBundle. By construction, this is NOT an opaque object. History April 2010: Arlindo da Silva arlindo.dasilva@nasa.gov 2026: Modernized and moved to base3g/ as part of MAPL3 migration The macros here are intended to simplify the process of\n accessing the per-gc private state via ESMF. Simple exception handling macros for MAPL. Short hand for declaring key variables Automatic exception hanler Try & catch exception functionality; the rc macro is similar\n to the RC=STATUS); _VERIFY(STATUS macro above but it does not invole the _VERIFY(STATUS)\n macro. Instead, it jumps out of the TRY block. Raising exceptions Pre-defined MAPL error codes The MAPL_ErrLog must be defined after MAPL_Exceptions The error logging may eventually evolve into a module based\n on the ESMF logger.  For now these macros provide simple\n traceback capability.\n new\n New\n Assumes status is passed back in dummy called “rc”\n Assumes “/home/runner/work/MAPL/MAPL/include/MAPL_ErrLog.h” and 130 are appropriate\n Old\n The error logging may eventually evolve into a module based\n on the ESMF logger.  For now these macros provide simple\n traceback capability.\n new\n New\n Assumes status is passed back in dummy called “rc”\n Assumes “/home/runner/work/MAPL/MAPL/include/MAPL_ErrLog.h” and 130 are appropriate\n Old\n The following macro causes a variable to appear to be “used”\n according to the compiler.  This is a kludge to avoid excessive\n warnings.  In most cases, a better fix would be to modify the the\n procedure interface, but it is impractical in the short term. Note that the conditional is never satisfied and a reasonable\n compiler will optimize the line away.  (Hopefully without\n reintroducing the warning!) Uses mapl_Comms_mod mapl_ArrayReductions_mod ESMF mapl_geom_api MAPL_Constants mapl_ErrorHandling_mod mapl_field_bundle_api module~~mapl_simplebundlemod_impl_mod~~UsesGraph module~mapl_simplebundlemod_impl_mod mapl_SimpleBundleMod_impl_mod ESMF ESMF module~mapl_simplebundlemod_impl_mod->ESMF module~mapl_arrayreductions_mod mapl_ArrayReductions_mod module~mapl_simplebundlemod_impl_mod->module~mapl_arrayreductions_mod module~mapl_comms_mod mapl_Comms_mod module~mapl_simplebundlemod_impl_mod->module~mapl_comms_mod module~mapl_constants MAPL_Constants module~mapl_simplebundlemod_impl_mod->module~mapl_constants module~mapl_errorhandling_mod mapl_ErrorHandling_mod module~mapl_simplebundlemod_impl_mod->module~mapl_errorhandling_mod module~mapl_field_bundle_api mapl_field_bundle_api module~mapl_simplebundlemod_impl_mod->module~mapl_field_bundle_api module~mapl_geom_api mapl_geom_api module~mapl_simplebundlemod_impl_mod->module~mapl_geom_api Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Used by module~~mapl_simplebundlemod_impl_mod~~UsedByGraph module~mapl_simplebundlemod_impl_mod mapl_SimpleBundleMod_impl_mod module~mapl_base_api mapl_base_api module~mapl_base_api->module~mapl_simplebundlemod_impl_mod module~mapl MAPL module~mapl->module~mapl_base_api Help Graph Key Nodes of different colours represent the following: Graph Key Module Module Submodule Submodule Subroutine Subroutine Function Function Program Program This Page's Entity This Page's Entity Solid arrows point from a submodule to the (sub)module which it is\ndescended from. Dashed arrows point from a module or program unit to \nmodules which it uses. Where possible, edges connecting nodes are\ngiven different colours to make them easier to distinguish in\nlarge graphs. Interfaces public        interface MAPL_SimpleBundleCreate private  function MAPL_SimpleBundleCreateEmpty(grid, rc, Levs, LevUnits, ptop, delp, name) result(self) Given inputs, create an empty SimpleBundle with coordinate arrays but no\ndata fields. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ESMF_Grid ), intent(in) :: grid integer, intent(out), optional :: rc real(kind=ESMF_KIND_R4), intent(in), optional :: Levs (:) Vertical coordinates character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: LevUnits Level units real(kind=ESMF_KIND_R4), intent(in), optional :: ptop top pressure (Pa) real(kind=ESMF_KIND_R4), intent(in), optional, pointer :: delp (:,:,:) layer thickness (Pa) character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: name Return Value type( MAPL_SimpleBundle ) private  function MAPL_SimpleBundleCreateFromBundle(Bundle, rc, Levs, LevUnits, ptop, delp, only_vars, strict, name) result(self) Given an ESMF Bundle, creates a corresponding Simple Bundle. The\nspecification of a vertical grid is optional but useful in many\ncases. The 1-D Levs will default to the layer number, and units of “1”.\nInput parameters (ptop,delp) can be used to record the corresponding\nLagrangian Control Volume Grid. When delp is not specified, variables DELP or delp are used if present inside the bundle. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type(ESMF_FieldBundle), intent(inout), target :: Bundle integer, intent(out), optional :: rc real(kind=ESMF_KIND_R4), intent(in), optional :: Levs (:) character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: LevUnits real(kind=ESMF_KIND_R4), intent(in), optional :: ptop real(kind=ESMF_KIND_R4), intent(in), optional, pointer :: delp (:,:,:) character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: only_vars comma-separated field names logical, intent(in), optional :: strict error if only_vars name not found character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: name Return Value type( MAPL_SimpleBundle ) private  function MAPL_SimpleBundleCreateFromState(State, rc, Levs, LevUnits, ptop, delp, only_vars, strict, name) result(self) Given an ESMF State, creates a corresponding Simple Bundle.\nIt is assumed that the ESMF State has a single grid. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( ESMF_State ), intent(inout), target :: State integer, intent(out), optional :: rc real(kind=ESMF_KIND_R4), intent(in), optional :: Levs (:) character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: LevUnits real(kind=ESMF_KIND_R4), intent(in), optional :: ptop real(kind=ESMF_KIND_R4), intent(in), optional, pointer :: delp (:,:,:) character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: only_vars logical, intent(in), optional :: strict character(len=*), intent(in), optional :: name Return Value type( MAPL_SimpleBundle ) Derived Types type, public :: MAPL_SimpleBundle Components Type Visibility Attributes Name Initial character(len=ESMF_MAXSTR), public :: name integer, public :: n1d = -1 integer, public :: n2d = -1 integer, public :: n3d = -1 logical, public :: bundleAlloc = .false. type( ESMF_Grid ), public :: grid Associated ESMF grid type(ESMF_FieldBundle), public, pointer :: Bundle => null() Associated ESMF bundle type(SimpleArray_1D), public, pointer :: r1 (:) => null() type(SimpleArray_2D), public, pointer :: r2 (:) => null() type(SimpleArray_3D), public, pointer :: r3 (:) => null() type(SimpleGrid), public :: coords Coordinate variables Functions public  function MAPL_SimpleBundleGetIndex (self, name, rank, rc, quiet) result(iq) Finds the index of the first variable with name vname .\nNote: comparison is case-sensitive (trim only). Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( MAPL_SimpleBundle ), intent(in) :: self character(len=*), intent(in) :: name integer, intent(in) :: rank integer, intent(out), optional :: rc logical, intent(in), optional :: quiet Return Value integer Subroutines public  subroutine MAPL_SimpleBundleDestroy (self, rc) Destructor for the MAPL Simple Bundle. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( MAPL_SimpleBundle ), intent(inout) :: self integer, intent(out), optional :: rc public  subroutine MAPL_SimpleBundlePrint (self, rc) Prints the global max/min for each variable in the Simple Bundle. Arguments Type Intent Optional Attributes Name type( MAPL_SimpleBundle ), intent(in) :: self integer, intent(out), optional :: rc","tags":"","url":"module/mapl_simplebundlemod_impl_mod.html"},{"title":"pFIO_MessageVisitorMod – MAPL","text":"Uses pFIO_AbstractMessageMod pFIO_AddWriteDataCollectionMessageMod pFIO_CollectiveStageDataMessageMod pFIO_ModifyMetadataMessageMod pFIO_DoneMessageMod pFIO_StageDataMessageMod pFIO_HandShakeMessageMod pFIO_AddReadDataCollectionMessageMod pFIO_StageDoneMessageMod pFIO_ReplaceMetadataMessageMod pFIO_DummyMessageMod pFIO_AbstractRequestHandleMod pFIO_CollectivePrefetchDoneMessageMod pFIO_CollectivePrefetchDataMessageMod pFIO_PrefetchDoneMessageMod pFIO_PrefetchDataMessageMod pFIO_IDMessageMod mapl_ErrorHandling_mod pFIO_CollectiveStageDoneMessageMod pFIO_TerminateMessageMod module~~pfio_messagevisitormod~~UsesGraph module~pfio_messagevisitormod pFIO_MessageVisitorMod module~mapl_errorhandling_mod mapl_ErrorHandling_mod module~pfio_messagevisitormod->module~mapl_errorhandling_mod module~pfio_abstractmessagemod pFIO_AbstractMessageMod module~pfio_messagevisitormod->module~pfio_abstractmessagemod module~pfio_abstractrequesthandlemod pFIO_AbstractRequestHandleMod module~pfio_messagevisitormod->module~pfio_abstractrequesthandlemod module~pfio_addreaddatacollectionmessagemod pFIO_AddReadDataCollectionMessageMod module~pfio_messagevisitormod->module~pfio_addreaddatacollectionmessagemod module~pfio_addwritedatacollectionmessagemod pFIO_Add